IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XVIII, ss 207 to 213: DISSOLUTION.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. How a corporation ends: by its directors or shareholders (s 210 for a corporation
-- with no business to wind up, s 211 for a voluntary liquidation and dissolution), by the Director (s 212),
-- or by a court (s 213). Section 209 brings a dissolved corporation back (revival). Section 208 takes an
-- insolvent or bankrupt corporation out of this Part. Court-supervised liquidation (ss 214 to 220) is in
-- cb4-court-liquidation.
--
-- "CEASES TO EXIST ON THE DATE SHOWN" (ss 210(6), 211(16), 212(4), 213(5)): the corporation exists
-- strictly BEFORE that date and not on it (fork F2, as for s 186.1(5)). "Becomes effective on the date
-- shown" (s 209(3.1), s 211(12)): on or after it.
--
-- Sections 262 (certificates), 246, 21.21(2), 16(2), 21, 157, 159 and 109(4) belong to other pieces; the
-- Criminal Code and the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act are not among the sources.

§§ `s 207 Definition of court`

-- src:2579 | PART XVIII Liquidation and Dissolution
-- src:2580 | Definition of court
-- src:2581 | 207 In this Part, court means a court having jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office.
@ref CBCA s 207 (src:2581)
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a court is the court of this Part within s 207` MEANS
    `the court has jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office`

§§ `s 208 Application of Part`

-- (1): this Part, other than ss 209 and 212, does not apply to an insolvent person or a bankrupt (as
-- defined in s 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act, which is not among the sources: plain inputs).
-- src:2582 | Application of Part
-- src:2583 | 208 (1) This Part, other than sections 209 and 212, does not apply to a corporation that is an insolvent person or a bankrupt as those terms are defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act.
@ref CBCA s 208(1) (src:2583)
GIVEN `the provision is section 209 or section 212` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Part applies to the corporation within s 208(1)` MEANS
        `the provision is section 209 or section 212`
    OR  (    (NOT `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act`)
         AND (NOT `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act`))

-- src:2584 | Staying proceedings
-- src:2585 | (2) Any proceedings taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve a corporation shall be stayed if the corporation is at any time found, in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act, to be an insolvent person as defined in section 2 of that Act.
@ref CBCA s 208(2) (src:2585)
GIVEN `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proceedings are stayed within s 208(2)` MEANS
        `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation`
    AND `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person`

§§ `s 209 Revival`

-- (1): the ways a body corporate may have been dissolved, and who may apply.
-- src:2586 | Revival
-- src:2587 | 209 (1) When a corporation or other body corporate is dissolved under this Part, section 268 of this Act, section 261 of the Canada Business Corporations Act, chapter 33 of the Statutes of Canada, 1974-75-76, or subsection 297(6) of the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act, any interested person may apply to the Director to have the dissolved corporation or other body corporate revived as a corporation under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 209(1) (src:2587)
DECLARE `Way a body corporate was dissolved for s 209(1)` IS ONE OF
    `dissolved under this Part`
    `dissolved under section 268 of this Act`
    `dissolved under section 261 of the Canada Business Corporations Act, chapter 33 of the Statutes of Canada, 1974-75-76`
    `dissolved under subsection 297(6) of the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act`
    `dissolved in some other way`

@ref CBCA s 209(1) (src:2587)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a body corporate was dissolved for s 209(1)`
      `the person is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an interested person may apply to the Director for revival within s 209(1)` MEANS
        `the person is an interested person`
    AND (CONSIDER way
         WHEN `dissolved in some other way` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- src:2588 | Articles of revival
-- src:2589 | (2) Articles of revival in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 209(2) (src:2589)
GIVEN `the articles of revival are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of revival have been sent as s 209(2) requires` MEANS
    `the articles of revival are in the form the Director fixes`

-- (3): the Director shall issue the certificate on receipt IF (a) the conditions precedent the Director
-- considers reasonable are fulfilled AND (b) there is no valid reason for refusing.
-- src:2590 | Certificate of revival
-- src:2591 | (3) On receipt of articles of revival, the Director shall issue a certificate of revival in accordance with section 262, if
-- src:2592 | (a) the dissolved corporation or other body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable; and
-- src:2593 | (b) there is no valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate.
@ref CBCA s 209(3) (src:2591-2593)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of revival` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of revival within s 209(3)` MEANS
        `the Director has received articles of revival`
    AND `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable`
    AND (NOT `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate`)

-- src:2594 | Date of revival
-- src:2595 | (3.1) The dissolved corporation or other body corporate is revived as a corporation under this Act on the date shown on the certificate of revival.
@ref CBCA s 209(3.1) (src:2595)
GIVEN `the date shown on the certificate of revival` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body corporate is revived as a corporation under this Act on a day within s 209(3.1)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown on the certificate of revival`

-- (4): the revived corporation is restored and liable "in the same manner and to the same extent as if it
-- had not been dissolved", subject to three things. Where one of them is in play the subsection does not
-- restore the position in that respect.
-- src:2596 | Rights and obligations preserved
-- src:2597 | (4) Subject to any reasonable terms that may be imposed by the Director, to the rights acquired by any person after its dissolution and to any changes to the internal affairs of the corporation or other body corporate after its dissolution, the revived corporation is, in the same manner and to the same extent as if it had not been dissolved,
-- src:2598 | (a) restored to its previous position in law, including the restoration of any rights and privileges whether arising before its dissolution or after its dissolution and before its revival; and
-- src:2599 | (b) liable for the obligations that it would have had if it had not been dissolved whether they arise before its dissolution or after its dissolution and before its revival.
@ref CBCA s 209(4) (src:2597-2599)
DECLARE `Matter that limits the restoration under s 209(4)` IS ONE OF
    `a reasonable term imposed by the Director`
    `a right acquired by a person after the dissolution`
    `a change to the internal affairs of the body corporate after its dissolution`
    `none of these`

@ref CBCA s 209(4)(a) (src:2597-2598)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been revived` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter that limits the restoration under s 209(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the revived corporation is restored to its previous position in respect of the matter within s 209(4)(a)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been revived`
    AND (CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `none of these` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

@ref CBCA s 209(4)(b) (src:2597 src:2599)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been revived` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter that limits the restoration under s 209(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the revived corporation is liable for the obligations it would have had in respect of the matter within s 209(4)(b)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been revived`
    AND (CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `none of these` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- src:2600 | Legal actions
-- src:2601 | (5) Any legal action respecting the affairs of a revived corporation taken between the time of its dissolution and its revival is valid and effective.
@ref CBCA s 209(5) (src:2601)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been revived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal action respecting its affairs was taken between its dissolution and its revival` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a legal action taken between dissolution and revival is valid and effective within s 209(5)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been revived`
    AND `the legal action respecting its affairs was taken between its dissolution and its revival`

-- (6): "interested person includes": a listed person is one (JUST TRUE); another is not decided (NOTHING).
-- src:2602 | Definition of interested person
-- src:2603 | (6) In this section, interested person includes
-- src:2604 | (a) a shareholder, a director, an officer, an employee and a creditor of the dissolved corporation or other body corporate;
-- src:2605 | (b) a person who has a contract — other than, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title — with the dissolved corporation or other body corporate;
-- src:2606 | (c) a person who, although at the time of dissolution of the corporation or other body corporate was not a person described in paragraph (a), would be such a person if a certificate of revival is issued under this section; and
-- src:2607 | (d) a trustee in bankruptcy or liquidator for the dissolved corporation or other body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 209(6) (src:2603-2607)
DECLARE `Kind of person named in s 209(6)` IS ONE OF
    `a shareholder of the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(a))`
    `a director of the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(a))`
    `an officer of the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(a))`
    `an employee of the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(a))`
    `a creditor of the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(a))`
    `a person who has a contract with the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(b))`
    `a person who would be such a person if a certificate of revival is issued (s 209(6)(c))`
    `a trustee in bankruptcy or liquidator for the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(d))`
    `a person not named in s 209(6)`

@ref CBCA s 209(6) (src:2603-2607)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person named in s 209(6)`
      `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether the person is an interested person within s 209(6)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a person not named in s 209(6)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a person who has a contract with the dissolved body corporate (s 209(6)(b))` THEN (IF `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 210 Dissolution by the corporation, without a liquidation`

-- src:2608 | Dissolution before commencing business
-- src:2609 | 210 (1) A corporation that has not issued any shares may be dissolved at any time by resolution of all the directors.
@ref CBCA s 210(1) (src:2609)
GIVEN `the corporation has issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may be dissolved by resolution of all the directors within s 210(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation has issued shares`)
    AND `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it`

-- The class vote of (2) and (3): "special resolutions of the holders of each class whether or not they are
-- otherwise entitled to vote": where the corporation has issued more than one class, the holders of EACH
-- class pass a special resolution (in place of the shareholders' special resolution). One class's tally:
-- src:2610 | Dissolution if no property
-- src:2611 | (2) A corporation that has no property and no liabilities may be dissolved by special resolution of the shareholders or, where it has issued more than one class of shares, by special resolutions of the holders of each class whether or not they are otherwise entitled to vote.
@ref CBCA s 210(2) (src:2611)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a class have approved the dissolution by special resolution within s 210(2)` MEANS
    `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally

@ref CBCA s 210(2) (src:2611)
GIVEN `the corporation has no property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has no liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `every class has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may be dissolved by special resolution within s 210(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation has no property`
    AND `the corporation has no liabilities`
    AND (    (    `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares`
              AND `every class has approved by special resolution`)
         OR  (    (NOT `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares`)
              AND `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally))

-- src:2612 | Dissolution where property disposed of
-- src:2613 | (3) A corporation that has property or liabilities or both may be dissolved by special resolution of the shareholders or, where it has issued more than one class of shares, by special resolutions of the holders of each class whether or not they are otherwise entitled to vote, if
-- src:2614 | (a) by the special resolution or resolutions the shareholders authorize the directors to cause the corporation to distribute any property and discharge any liabilities; and
-- src:2615 | (b) the corporation has distributed any property and discharged any liabilities before it sends articles of dissolution to the Director pursuant to subsection (4).
@ref CBCA s 210(3) (src:2613-2615)
GIVEN `the corporation has property or liabilities or both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `every class has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions authorize the directors to cause the corporation to distribute any property and discharge any liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation distributed its property and discharged its liabilities before sending articles of dissolution to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may be dissolved by special resolution within s 210(3)` MEANS
        `the corporation has property or liabilities or both`
    AND (    (    `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares`
              AND `every class has approved by special resolution`)
         OR  (    (NOT `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares`)
              AND `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally))
    AND `the resolutions authorize the directors to cause the corporation to distribute any property and discharge any liabilities`
    AND `the corporation distributed its property and discharged its liabilities before sending articles of dissolution to the Director`

-- src:2616 | Articles of dissolution
-- src:2617 | (4) Articles of dissolution in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 210(4) (src:2617)
GIVEN `the articles of dissolution are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of dissolution have been sent as s 210(4) requires` MEANS
    `the articles of dissolution are in the form the Director fixes`

-- src:2618 | Certificate of dissolution
-- src:2619 | (5) On receipt of articles of dissolution, the Director shall issue a certificate of dissolution in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 210(5) (src:2619)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of dissolution within s 210(5)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of dissolution`

-- src:2620 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2621 | (6) The corporation ceases to exist on the date shown in the certificate of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 210(6) (src:2621)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation exists on a day within s 210(6)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution`

§§ `s 211 Voluntary liquidation and dissolution`

-- (1): the directors may propose; a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting may make a proposal
-- "in accordance with section 137" (piece cb3).
-- src:2622 | Proposing liquidation and dissolution
-- src:2623 | 211 (1) The directors may propose, or a shareholder who is entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders may, in accordance with section 137, make a proposal for, the voluntary liquidation and dissolution of a corporation.
@ref CBCA s 211(1) (src:2623)
GIVEN `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 137 (piece cb3)
      `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may propose voluntary liquidation and dissolution within s 211(1)` MEANS
        `the person is a director`
    OR  (    `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders`
         AND `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137`)

-- src:2624 | Notice of meeting
-- src:2625 | (2) Notice of any meeting of shareholders at which voluntary liquidation and dissolution is to be proposed shall set out the terms thereof.
@ref CBCA s 211(2) (src:2625)
GIVEN `the notice sets out the terms of the voluntary liquidation and dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting complies within s 211(2)` MEANS
    `the notice sets out the terms of the voluntary liquidation and dissolution`

-- src:2626 | Shareholders resolution
-- src:2627 | (3) A corporation may liquidate and dissolve by special resolution of the shareholders or, where the corporation has issued more than one class of shares, by special resolutions of the holders of each class whether or not they are otherwise entitled to vote.
@ref CBCA s 211(3) (src:2627)
GIVEN `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `every class has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may liquidate and dissolve within s 211(3)` MEANS
        (    `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares`
         AND `every class has approved by special resolution`)
    OR  (    (NOT `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares`)
         AND `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally)

@ref CBCA s 211(3) (src:2627)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a class have approved the liquidation and dissolution by special resolution within s 211(3)` MEANS
    `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally

-- src:2628 | Statement of intent to dissolve
-- src:2629 | (4) A statement of intent to dissolve in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 211(4) (src:2629)
GIVEN `the statement of intent to dissolve is in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the statement of intent to dissolve has been sent as s 211(4) requires` MEANS
    `the statement of intent to dissolve is in the form the Director fixes`

-- src:2630 | Certificate of intent to dissolve
-- src:2631 | (5) On receipt of a statement of intent to dissolve, the Director shall issue a certificate of intent to dissolve in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 211(5) (src:2631)
GIVEN `the Director has received a statement of intent to dissolve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of intent to dissolve within s 211(5)` MEANS
    `the Director has received a statement of intent to dissolve`

-- (6): after the certificate of intent, the corporation carries on business only as the liquidation needs.
-- Its corporate existence continues until the Director issues a certificate of dissolution; subsection (16)
-- says it ceases to exist on the date SHOWN in that certificate (see the register).
-- src:2632 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2633 | (6) On issue of a certificate of intent to dissolve, the corporation shall cease to carry on business except to the extent necessary for the liquidation, but its corporate existence continues until the Director issues a certificate of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 211(6) (src:2633)
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is necessary for the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may carry on the business within s 211(6)` MEANS
        (NOT `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued`)
    OR  `the business is necessary for the liquidation`

-- src:2634 | Liquidation
-- src:2635 | (7) After issue of a certificate of intent to dissolve, the corporation shall
-- src:2636 | (a) immediately cause notice thereof to be sent to each known creditor of the corporation;
@ref CBCA s 211(7)(a) (src:2636)
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must immediately notify each known creditor within s 211(7)(a)` MEANS
    `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued`

-- src:2637 | (b) without delay take reasonable steps to give notice of it in each province in Canada where the corporation was carrying on business at the time it sent the statement of intent to dissolve to the Director;
@ref CBCA s 211(7)(b) (src:2637)
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation was carrying on business in the province when it sent the statement of intent to dissolve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must take reasonable steps to give notice in the province within s 211(7)(b)` MEANS
        `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued`
    AND `the corporation was carrying on business in the province when it sent the statement of intent to dissolve`

-- src:2638 | (c) proceed to collect its property, to dispose of properties that are not to be distributed in kind to its shareholders, to discharge all its obligations and to do all other acts required to liquidate its business; and
@ref CBCA s 211(7)(c) (src:2638)
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must proceed to collect its property and liquidate its business within s 211(7)(c)` MEANS
    `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued`

-- src:2639 | (d) after giving the notice required under paragraphs (a) and (b) and adequately providing for the payment or discharge of all its obligations, distribute its remaining property, either in money or in kind, among its shareholders according to their respective rights.
@ref CBCA s 211(7)(d) (src:2639)
GIVEN `the corporation has given the notices required by paragraphs 211(7)(a) and 211(7)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has adequately provided for the payment or discharge of all its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation shall distribute its remaining property among its shareholders within s 211(7)(d)` MEANS
        `the corporation has given the notices required by paragraphs 211(7)(a) and 211(7)(b)`
    AND `the corporation has adequately provided for the payment or discharge of all its obligations`

-- src:2640 | Supervision by court
-- src:2641 | (8) The Director or any interested person may, at any time during the liquidation of a corporation, apply to a court for an order that the liquidation be continued under the supervision of the court as provided in this Part, and on such application the court may so order and make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 211(8) (src:2641)
GIVEN `the applicant is the Director or an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made during the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director or an interested person may apply for the court's supervision within s 211(8)` MEANS
        `the applicant is the Director or an interested person`
    AND `the application is made during the liquidation`

@ref CBCA s 211(8) (src:2641)
GIVEN `an application for supervision has been made during the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order supervision and make any further order it thinks fit within s 211(8)` MEANS
    `an application for supervision has been made during the liquidation`

-- src:2642 | Notice to Director
-- src:2643 | (9) An applicant under this section shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 211(9) (src:2643)
GIVEN `the person has applied under section 211` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 211(9)` MEANS
    `the person has applied under section 211`

@ref CBCA s 211(9) (src:2643)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 211` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 211(9)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under section 211`

-- (10): revocation: after the certificate of intent and before the certificate of dissolution, by a
-- statement in the Director's form, if approved in the same manner as the (3) resolution.
-- src:2644 | Revocation
-- src:2645 | (10) At any time after issue of a certificate of intent to dissolve and before issue of a certificate of dissolution, a certificate of intent to dissolve may be revoked by sending to the Director a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve in the form that the Director fixes, if such revocation is approved in the same manner as the resolution under subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 211(10) (src:2645)
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of dissolution has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement of revocation is in the form the Director fixes and has been sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revocation is approved in the same manner as the resolution under subsection 211(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificate of intent to dissolve may be revoked within s 211(10)` MEANS
        `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued`
    AND (NOT `a certificate of dissolution has been issued`)
    AND `the statement of revocation is in the form the Director fixes and has been sent`
    AND `the revocation is approved in the same manner as the resolution under subsection 211(3)`

-- src:2646 | Certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve
-- src:2647 | (11) On receipt of a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve, the Director shall issue a certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 211(11) (src:2647)
GIVEN `the Director has received a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve within s 211(11)` MEANS
    `the Director has received a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve`

-- src:2648 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2649 | (12) On the date shown in the certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve, the revocation is effective and the corporation may continue to carry on its business or businesses.
@ref CBCA s 211(12) (src:2649)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the revocation is effective and the corporation may continue its business on a day within s 211(12)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve`

-- src:2650 | Right to dissolve
-- src:2651 | (13) If a certificate of intent to dissolve has not been revoked and the corporation has complied with subsection (7), the corporation shall prepare articles of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 211(13) (src:2651)
GIVEN `the certificate of intent to dissolve has not been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has complied with subsection 211(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation shall prepare articles of dissolution within s 211(13)` MEANS
        `the certificate of intent to dissolve has not been revoked`
    AND `the corporation has complied with subsection 211(7)`

-- src:2652 | Articles of dissolution
-- src:2653 | (14) Articles of dissolution in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 211(14) (src:2653)
GIVEN `the articles of dissolution are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of dissolution have been sent as s 211(14) requires` MEANS
    `the articles of dissolution are in the form the Director fixes`

-- src:2654 | Certificate of dissolution
-- src:2655 | (15) On receipt of articles of dissolution, the Director shall issue a certificate of dissolution in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 211(15) (src:2655)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of dissolution within s 211(15)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of dissolution`

-- src:2656 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2657 | (16) The corporation ceases to exist on the date shown in the certificate of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 211(16) (src:2657)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation exists on a day within s 211(16)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution`

§§ `s 212 Dissolution by the Director`

-- (1)(a): five grounds. Each is its own rule; the last rule of this block says whether any one holds.
-- src:2658 | Dissolution by Director
-- src:2659 | 212 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), the Director may
-- src:2660 | (a) dissolve a corporation by issuing a certificate of dissolution under this section on the grounds that
-- src:2661 | (i) the corporation has not commenced business within three years after the date shown in its certificate of incorporation,
@ref CBCA s 212(1)(a)(i) (src:2661)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the corporation has commenced business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the corporation commenced business` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has not commenced business within three years after the date shown in its certificate of incorporation on a day within s 212(1)(a)(i)` MEANS
        `the day asked about` GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 3, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation`)
    AND (NOT (    `the corporation has commenced business`
              AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 3, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation` `the day the corporation commenced business`))

-- src:2662 | (ii) the corporation has not carried on its business for three consecutive years,
@ref CBCA s 212(1)(a)(ii) (src:2662)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive years the corporation has not carried on its business` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has not carried on its business for three consecutive years within s 212(1)(a)(ii)` MEANS
    `the number of consecutive years the corporation has not carried on its business` AT LEAST 3

-- (iii): "in default for a period of one year": the ground exists from the first anniversary of the day the
-- default began (fork F5).
-- src:2663 | (iii) the corporation is in default for a period of one year in sending to the Director any fee or any notice, document or other information required by this Act,
@ref CBCA s 212(1)(a)(iii) (src:2663)
GIVEN `the day the default began` IS A DATE
      `the default is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is in default for one year in sending a fee, notice, document or information within s 212(1)(a)(iii)` MEANS
        `the default is continuing`
    AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 1, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` `the day the default began`)

-- src:2664 | (iv) the corporation does not have any directors or is in the situation described in subsection 109(4), or
@ref CBCA s 212(1)(a)(iv) (src:2664)
GIVEN `the corporation does not have any directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: subsection 109(4) (piece cb2)
      `the corporation is in the situation described in subsection 109(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has no directors or is in the situation of s 109(4) within s 212(1)(a)(iv)` MEANS
        `the corporation does not have any directors`
    OR  `the corporation is in the situation described in subsection 109(4)`

-- src:2665 | (v) the Director is notified by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness that the corporation is a listed entity as defined in subsection 83.01(1) of the Criminal Code; or
@ref CBCA s 212(1)(a)(v) (src:2665)
GIVEN `the Director is notified by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness that the corporation is a listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is a listed entity notified to the Director within s 212(1)(a)(v)` MEANS
    `the Director is notified by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness that the corporation is a listed entity`

@ref CBCA s 212(1)(a) (src:2660-2665)
GIVEN `ground (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ground (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ground (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ground (iv)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ground (v)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may dissolve the corporation on a ground within s 212(1)(a)` MEANS
        `ground (i)`
    OR  `ground (ii)`
    OR  `ground (iii)`
    OR  `ground (iv)`
    OR  `ground (v)`

-- src:2666 | (b) apply to a court for an order dissolving the corporation, in which case section 217 applies.
@ref CBCA s 212(1)(b) (src:2666)
GIVEN `the Director acts under section 212(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may apply to a court for an order dissolving the corporation within s 212(1)(b)` MEANS
    `the Director acts under section 212(1)`

-- (2) and (2.1): 120 days' notice to the corporation and each director, and publication; none of that for
-- the listed-entity ground.
-- src:2667 | Publication
-- src:2668 | (2) The Director shall not dissolve a corporation under this section until the Director has
-- src:2669 | (a) given one hundred and twenty days notice of the decision to dissolve the corporation to the corporation and to each director thereof; and
-- src:2670 | (b) published notice of that decision in a publication generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 212(2) (src:2668-2670)
GIVEN `the Director gave one hundred and twenty days notice of the decision to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director gave that notice to each director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director published notice of the decision in a publication generally available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director has met the conditions of s 212(2)` MEANS
        `the Director gave one hundred and twenty days notice of the decision to the corporation`
    AND `the Director gave that notice to each director`
    AND `the Director published notice of the decision in a publication generally available to the public`

-- src:2671 | Exception — listed entities
-- src:2672 | (2.1) Subsection (2) does not apply if the ground, or one of the grounds, for issuing a certificate of dissolution is the ground set out in subparagraph (1)(a)(v).
@ref CBCA s 212(2.1) (src:2672)
GIVEN `one of the grounds is the ground in subparagraph 212(1)(a)(v)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 212(2) applies within s 212(2.1)` MEANS
    NOT `one of the grounds is the ground in subparagraph 212(1)(a)(v)`

-- (2)(a), (3): the notice period is 120 days from the day the notice is given; the certificate is "not to be
-- issued until after the end" of it, so the earliest day is the day after the 120th.
@ref CBCA s 212(2), s 212(3) (src:2669 src:2674)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the certificate of dissolution may be issued within s 212(3)` MEANS
    (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 120, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the notice was given`) PLUS 1

-- src:2673 | Certificate of dissolution
-- src:2674 | (3) Unless cause to the contrary has been shown or an order has been made by a court under section 246, the Director may issue a certificate of dissolution in the form that the Director fixes. However, if subsection (2) applies, the certificate is not to be issued until after the end of the period referred to in that subsection.
@ref CBCA s 212(3) (src:2674)
GIVEN `cause to the contrary has been shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 246 (piece cb5)
      `a court has made an order under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 212(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may issue a certificate of dissolution on a day within s 212(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `cause to the contrary has been shown`)
    AND (NOT `a court has made an order under section 246`)
    AND (    (NOT `subsection 212(2) applies`)
         OR  `the day I am asking about` AT LEAST (`the earliest day the certificate of dissolution may be issued within s 212(3)` `the day the notice was given`))

-- src:2675 | Payment of incorporation fee or sending of information
-- src:2676 | (3.1) Despite anything in this section, the Director may dissolve a corporation by issuing a certificate of dissolution if the required fee for the issuance of a certificate of incorporation has not been paid or if the corporation has not complied with subsection 21.21(2).
@ref CBCA s 212(3.1) (src:2676)
GIVEN `the required fee for the issuance of a certificate of incorporation has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: subsection 21.21(2) (piece cb1)
      `the corporation has not complied with subsection 21.21(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may dissolve the corporation despite the rest of s 212 within s 212(3.1)` MEANS
        `the required fee for the issuance of a certificate of incorporation has not been paid`
    OR  `the corporation has not complied with subsection 21.21(2)`

-- src:2677 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2678 | (4) The corporation ceases to exist on the date shown in the certificate of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 212(4) (src:2678)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation exists on a day within s 212(4)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution`

§§ `s 213 Dissolution by a court`

-- (1)(a): "two or more consecutive years" of not holding annual meetings as the Act requires.
-- src:2679 | Grounds for dissolution
-- src:2680 | 213 (1) The Director or any interested person may apply to a court for an order dissolving a corporation if the corporation has
-- src:2681 | (a) failed for two or more consecutive years to comply with the requirements of this Act with respect to the holding of annual meetings of shareholders;
-- src:2682 | (b) contravened subsection 16(2) or section 21, 157 or 159; or
-- src:2683 | (c) procured any certificate under this Act by misrepresentation.
@ref CBCA s 213(1) (src:2680-2683)
GIVEN `the applicant is the Director or an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of consecutive years the corporation has failed to comply with the requirements about annual meetings` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: subsection 16(2), sections 21, 157 and 159 (pieces cb1 and cb3)
      `the corporation has contravened subsection 16(2) or section 21, 157 or 159` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has procured a certificate under this Act by misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director or an interested person may apply to a court for an order dissolving the corporation within s 213(1)` MEANS
        `the applicant is the Director or an interested person`
    AND (    `the number of consecutive years the corporation has failed to comply with the requirements about annual meetings` AT LEAST 2
         OR  `the corporation has contravened subsection 16(2) or section 21, 157 or 159`
         OR  `the corporation has procured a certificate under this Act by misrepresentation`)

-- src:2684 | Notice to Director
-- src:2685 | (2) An applicant under this section shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 213(2) (src:2685)
GIVEN `the person has applied under section 213` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 213(2)` MEANS
    `the person has applied under section 213`

@ref CBCA s 213(2) (src:2685)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 213` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 213(2)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under section 213`

-- src:2686 | Dissolution order
-- src:2687 | (3) On an application under this section or section 212, the court may order that the corporation be dissolved or that the corporation be liquidated and dissolved under the supervision of the court, and the court may make any other order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 213(3) (src:2687)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 213 or 212` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order within s 213(3)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under section 213 or 212`

-- src:2688 | Certificate
-- src:2689 | (4) On receipt of an order under this section, section 212 or 214, the Director shall
-- src:2690 | (a) if the order is to dissolve the corporation, issue a certificate of dissolution in the form that the Director fixes; or
-- src:2691 | (b) if the order is to liquidate and dissolve the corporation under the supervision of the court, issue a certificate of intent to dissolve in the form that the Director fixes and publish notice of the order in a publication generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 213(4) (src:2689-2691)
DECLARE `Kind of order the Director receives under s 213(4)` IS ONE OF
    `an order to dissolve the corporation`
    `an order to liquidate and dissolve the corporation under the supervision of the court`
    `an order of another kind than those s 213(4) names`

DECLARE `What the Director must do on receiving an order under s 213(4)` IS ONE OF
    `to issue a certificate of dissolution in the form the Director fixes`
    `to issue a certificate of intent to dissolve in the form the Director fixes and publish notice of the order in a publication generally available to the public`
    `the Act does not say what the Director must do`

@ref CBCA s 213(4) (src:2689-2691)
GIVEN order IS A `Kind of order the Director receives under s 213(4)`
GIVETH A `What the Director must do on receiving an order under s 213(4)`
`what the Director must do on receiving an order within s 213(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `an order to dissolve the corporation` THEN `to issue a certificate of dissolution in the form the Director fixes`
    WHEN `an order to liquidate and dissolve the corporation under the supervision of the court` THEN `to issue a certificate of intent to dissolve in the form the Director fixes and publish notice of the order in a publication generally available to the public`
    WHEN `an order of another kind than those s 213(4) names` THEN `the Act does not say what the Director must do`

-- src:2692 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2693 | (5) The corporation ceases to exist on the date shown in the certificate of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 213(5) (src:2693)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation exists on a day within s 213(5)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution`
